            "CONTINUATION HAND-OFF\n\nUNIVERSAL OPERATING CONTRACT — MASTER v6\n\nACKNOWLEDGEMENT GATE\n\nOperating Contract: ACKNOWLEDGED\n\nChat Classification: CONTINUATION CHAT\n\nAlways-Included Context Status: PARTIALLY KNOWN\n\nGovernance Status: IN PROGRESS\n\nAuthority Boundaries: ACKNOWLEDGED\n\nHand-Off Semantics: ACKNOWLEDGED\n\nContinuation Signal Behavior: ACKNOWLEDGED\n\nNo-Memory-Assumption Rule: ACKNOWLEDGED\n\nRepository Gate: NOT APPLICABLE\n\nCommand-First Rule: NOT APPLICABLE\n\nStep Discipline: ACKNOWLEDGED\n\nPROJECT-SPECIFIC POPULATION BLOCK\n\nPROJECT NAME:\n\nKnowledge Governance Infrastructure (KGI)\n\nSUBSYSTEM NAME:\n\nProject Continuity & Ecosystem Discovery\n\nCHAT TYPE:\n\nCONTINUATION CHAT\n\nPHASE:\n\nDESIGN\n\nPROJECT CHARTER:\n\nKGI is a governance framework for transforming evidence into validated, traceable, continuity-preserving knowledge.\n\nMISSION STATEMENT:\n\nRecover knowledge.\nAudit assumptions.\nDiscover structure.\nReduce drift.\nCreate an evidence-backed ecosystem map.\n\nGOVERNANCE STATUS:\n\nIN PROGRESS\n\nIMMUTABLE DECISIONS:\n\nRaw evidence is authoritative.\nRaw evidence is immutable.\nHuman review remains authoritative.\nUnknown is preferred over guessing.\nRouting does not imply ownership.\nGovernance decisions must be traceable.\nEvidence is preserved before interpretation.\nDescriptive context does not override authoritative artifacts.\nKGI governs information before it is retrieved.\nChat Sorter is the first implementation of KGI.\n\nEXPLICITLY FORBIDDEN CHANGES:\n\nEditing raw evidence.\nInventing evidence.\nAssuming ownership from routing.\nTreating retrieval as governance.\nTreating hand-offs as completion.\nSkipping review.\nSkipping validation.\nAssuming ecosystem structure without evidence.\nRedesigning KGI during continuity discovery.\n\nAUTHORITY BOUNDARIES — MAY:\n\nReview audited KGI results.\nAnalyze KGI objectives.\nDesign future KGI architecture.\nIdentify missing layers between routing and ecosystem intelligence.\nPropose evidence-preserving continuity mechanisms.\nPropose ecosystem discovery mechanisms.\nDesign future artifact architecture.\nDesign future review workflows.\nIdentify knowledge-recovery opportunities.\n\nAUTHORITY BOUNDARIES — MAY NOT:\n\nInvent evidence.\nModify prior audit outcomes.\nAssume project identity without evidence.\nAutomatically merge projects.\nAutomatically merge concepts.\nAutomatically create ecosystem subsystems.\nTreat overlap detection as authority.\nTreat continuity suggestions as decisions.\nRedesign existing governance findings without authorization.\n\nCURRENT AUTHORITATIVE STATE:\n\nRepository checkpoint audit completed.\n\nGovernance findings audited:\n\nGOVFIND-000001 → RETAIN WITH NARROWING\nGOVFIND-000002 → REVISE / NARROW\nGOVFIND-000003 → RETAIN WITH MINOR NARROWING\nGOVFIND-000004 → RETAIN\nGOVFIND-000005 → RETAIN\nGOVFIND-000006 → RETAIN\nGOVFIND-000007 → RETAIN\nGOVFIND-000008 → RETAIN\nGOVFIND-000009 → RETAIN WITH MINOR NARROWING\n\nChats audited without findings:\n\nCHAT-000007\nCHAT-000009\nCHAT-000012\nCHAT-000013\nCHAT-000015\n\nMeta-audit completed.\n\nCURRENT DESCRIPTIVE CONTEXT:\n\nThe audit established that extraction, review, routing, and governance findings are generally functioning correctly.\n\nThe audit did not reveal widespread false positives.\n\nThe primary recurring issue observed was concern-type conflation, where findings occasionally broadened beyond the specific concern directly evidenced.\n\nA more important realization emerged during the audit:\n\nThe original user objective is not governance findings.\n\nThe original user objective is project continuity, knowledge recovery, ecosystem discovery, overlap detection, and prevention of cross-project contamination.\n\nThe user described a desired future workflow:\n\nComplete a chat.\nProcess the full chat through KGI.\nRoute relevant information to affected projects.\nUpdate project-specific knowledge.\nProduce clean continuation context for future project chats.\nDetect forgotten project names, renamed projects, duplicated projects, overlapping systems, and recurring capabilities.\nSurface review-required continuity alerts.\nDiscover shared subsystems and ecosystem structure through evidence-backed analysis.\n\nThe user specifically identified interest in:\n\nforgotten project names\nproject identity continuity\noverlap detection\nduplicate capability detection\nshared subsystem discovery\necosystem-level capability discovery\nproject relationship mapping\n\nOPEN AMBIGUITIES:\n\nHow project knowledge should be represented.\nHow continuity records should be represented.\nHow overlap records should be represented.\nHow ecosystem records should be represented.\nHow confidence scoring should operate.\nHow review workflows should operate.\nHow project rename detection should operate.\nHow duplicate-project detection should operate.\nHow subsystem-discovery evidence thresholds should operate.\nHow ecosystem maps should be generated and maintained.\n\nDRIFT RISKS:\n\nTreating overlap as equivalence.\nTreating similarity as identity.\nAutomatically merging projects.\nAutomatically creating subsystems.\nAllowing ecosystem discovery to become authority.\nAllowing continuity suggestions to become decisions.\nReplacing human review with inference.\nCreating ecosystem structure without evidence.\n\nNEXT VALID ACTION:\n\nDesign the architecture that transforms:\n\nRaw Chat\n→ Extraction Report\n→ Review Record\n→ Routing Packet\n\ninto:\n\nProject Knowledge\n→ Continuity Intelligence\n→ Overlap Detection\n→ Ecosystem Discovery\n\nwhile preserving authority boundaries, review requirements, evidence traceability, and human decision authority.\n\nREPOSITORY PATH, IF APPLICABLE:\n\nNOT APPLICABLE\n\nREPOSITORY SNAPSHOT, IF APPLICABLE:\n\nNOT APPLICABLE\n\nFULL-FILE POLICY:\n\nUNKNOWN\n\nHAND-OFF TYPE:\n\nCONTINUATION\n\nAUTHORITATIVE VS DESCRIPTIVE DISTINCTION\n\nAUTHORITATIVE\n\nKGI charter\nMission statement\nImmutable decisions\nGovernance finding audit dispositions\nMeta-audit conclusions\nAudit evidence\nExisting KGI artifacts\nExisting routing architecture\nExisting review architecture\n\nDESCRIPTIVE\n\nFuture continuity architecture\nFuture ecosystem architecture\nFuture subsystem-discovery concepts\nFuture overlap-detection concepts\nFuture project-identity concepts\nFuture artifact proposals\nFuture workflow proposals\n\nDESIGN OBJECTIVE\n\nThis chat is not implementing KGI.\n\nThis chat is not redesigning prior audits.\n\nThis chat is not processing additional chats.\n\nThis chat is designing the next major KGI layer:\n\nProject Continuity & Ecosystem Discovery.\n\nPrimary design question:\n\nHow should KGI transform reviewed and routed evidence into:\n\nproject continuity\nproject knowledge\noverlap detection\nduplicate-project detection\nproject rename detection\nsubsystem discovery\necosystem intelligence\n\nwhile preserving:\n\nevidence authority\nhuman review authority\ntraceability\nauditability\nunknown preservation\ngovernance boundaries\n\nHAND-OFF TYPE:\n\nCONTINUATION\n\nCONTINUATION HAND-OFF COMPLETE — AWAITING NEXT CHAT\n\n\nwhat is the point of this chat?"
