            "The point of this chat, based on the hand-off, is to design the layer that comes **after governance review is complete**.\n\nUp to this point, KGI has primarily proven:\n\n1. Raw chats can be preserved.\n2. Information can be extracted.\n3. Human review can validate or reject extraction.\n4. Information can be routed.\n5. Governance findings can be audited.\n\nWhat has *not* been designed yet is what happens **after routing**.\n\nThe hand-off explicitly identifies the realization that emerged during the audit:\n\n> The user's actual objective is not governance findings.\n\nGovernance findings are merely a safety mechanism.\n\nThe actual objective is:\n\n- project continuity\n- knowledge recovery\n- ecosystem discovery\n- overlap detection\n- forgotten project recovery\n- project identity preservation\n- cross-project contamination prevention\n\nSo the purpose of this chat is to answer:\n\n> Once a reviewed fact has been routed somewhere, how does KGI turn that routed evidence into usable continuity intelligence?\n\nOr more concretely:\n\nCurrent KGI:\n\n```text\nRaw Chat\n    ↓\nExtraction\n    ↓\nReview\n    ↓\nRouting\n```\n\nMissing KGI:\n\n```text\nRouting\n    ↓\nProject Knowledge\n    ↓\nContinuity Intelligence\n    ↓\nOverlap Detection\n    ↓\nEcosystem Discovery\n```\n\nThe questions this chat is supposed to answer are things like:\n\n### Project Knowledge\n\nHow does a project accumulate knowledge over time?\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nTranslAItor\n    CHAT-000032\n    CHAT-000109\n    CHAT-000284\n    CHAT-000711\n```\n\nWhat artifact actually represents the current state of knowledge for TranslAItor?\n\n---\n\n### Continuity Intelligence\n\nHow do we detect:\n\n```text\nYou talked about this six months ago.\n```\n\nor\n\n```text\nThis project already solved this problem.\n```\n\nor\n\n```text\nThis decision contradicts a previous decision.\n```\n\n---\n\n### Rename Detection\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nProject A\n```\n\nlater becomes\n\n```text\nProject B\n```\n\nwithout anyone realizing they are the same thing.\n\nHow does KGI surface:\n\n```text\nPossible project rename.\nHuman review required.\n```\n\nwithout automatically merging them?\n\n---\n\n### Duplicate Project Detection\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nSystem X\n```\n\nand\n\n```text\nSystem Y\n```\n\nboth claim to:\n\n```text\nPerform evidence routing.\n```\n\nHow does KGI detect the overlap and surface it for review?\n\n---\n\n### Shared Subsystem Discovery\n\nThis is the realization you described during the audit.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nProject A uses identity management.\n\nProject B uses identity management.\n\nProject C uses identity management.\n```\n\nKGI should eventually be able to say:\n\n```text\nRecurring capability detected.\n\nPotential shared subsystem candidate.\n\nReview required.\n```\n\nwithout deciding that it actually *is* a subsystem.\n\n---\n\n### Ecosystem Discovery\n\nEventually KGI should be able to produce something like:\n\n```text\nTranslAItor\n    └─ depends on Trust Framework\n\nNarrAIator\n    └─ depends on Identity Framework\n\nPEIS\n    └─ depends on Capability Registry\n\nAI Diagnostician\n    └─ depends on Capability Registry\n```\n\nand reveal ecosystem structure that emerged from evidence.\n\nNot because someone manually drew it.\n\nBecause the evidence repeatedly pointed to it.\n\n---\n\nSo, in one sentence:\n\n**The point of this chat is to design the layer that converts validated routed evidence into project memory, continuity intelligence, overlap detection, and ecosystem discovery while preserving human authority and evidence traceability.**\n\nThat is the major layer that currently does not exist in KGI."
          ]
