                "snippet": "PROJECT: Aletheia Forensis\nSUBSYSTEM: Subsystem 3 — Quality Assessment (PQ / EC)\nCHAT: Subsystem 3b — IMPLEMENTATION (AUTHORITATIVE)\n\nSTATUS:\n- DESIGN COMPLETE\n- GOVERNANCE LOCKED\n- THIS CHAT IS FOR IMPLEMENTATION ONLY\n\nAUTHORITATIVE DESIGN SOURCE:\n- Subsystem 3 Design / Specification Chat (Chat 3)\n- No new design decisions permitted here\n- Any deviation requires reopening Chat 3 explicitly\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nCORE PURPOSE (LOCKED)\n────────────────────────────────────────\nSubsystem 3 determines objective audiovisual quality for files of the\nsame movie identity, using only authoritative, immutable evidence.\n\nIt answers:\n“Given the same movie identity, which version is better, and why?”\n\nIt does NOT:\n- determine identity\n- detect duplicates\n- perform actions\n- use metadata as a quality proxy\n- force decisions under uncertainty\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nGLOBAL GOVERNANCE (APPLIES IN FULL)\n────────────────────────────────────────\nThe following governance rules are fully enforced:\n\n- Evidence Snapshot Binding (LOCKED)\n- Schema Compatibility & Version Enforcement (LOCKED)\n- Stop-State Algebra (LOCKED)\n- Authoritative vs Descriptive Data (LOCKED)\n- Advisory Non-Authority (LOCKED)\n- Determinism Envelope & Reproducibility (LOCKED)\n- No Raw Logs as Authority (LOCKED)\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nQUALITY MODEL (LOCKED)\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\nPlayback Quality (PQ):\n- Objective, ordinal: HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW | UNKNOWN\n- Derived ONLY from authoritative EvidenceObjects\n- Visual quality dominates audio quality\n- Monotonic: once assigned, PQ MUST NOT downgrade\n- Downgrade attempt ⇒ HARD_STOP (PQ_MONOTONICITY_VIOLATION)\n\nEvidence Completeness (EC):\n- Penalty-based confidence measure\n- Driven entirely by PolicySnapshot (no hardcoded penalties)\n- Penalizes missing probes, ambiguity, unreadable streams, conflicts\n- EC may change as evidence changes\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nPQ SIGNAL ENUMERATION (LOCKED)\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\nVisual PQ signals (dominant):\n- Resolution & sampling\n- Dynamic range & color fidelity (HDR, bit depth, transfer)\n- Compression / encode fidelity (only when authoritatively reported)\n- Structural correctness (primary stream presence)\n- Observable defects (decode errors, corruption)\n\nAudio PQ signals (secondary):\n- Codec fidelity\n- Channel layout\n- Sample rate / bit depth (when meaningful)\n- Integrity defects (dropouts, decode errors)\n\nPROHIBITED:\n- filenames, paths, metadata tags\n- file size or bitrate as proxy (unless policy allows narrowly)\n- release/source labels\n- advisory or heuristic scores\n\nMinimum evidence required per channel; otherwise PQ = UNKNOWN.\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nCOMPARISON RULES (LOCKED)\n────────────────────────────────────────\nWhen comparing files of the same identity:\n\n1. If PQ is decisively different → higher PQ wins\n2. If PQ equal or not comparable → higher EC wins\n3. If PQ and EC both equal → INDISTINGUISHABLE\n4. If evidence insufficient → UNKNOWN\n\nAllowed outcomes:\n- WINNER\n- LOSER\n- INDISTINGUISHABLE\n- UNKNOWN\n\nNo forced winner under ambiguity.\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nSAFETY-COMPATIBLE OUTPUTS (LOCKED)\n────────────────────────────────────────\nQualityObjects MUST be safe for Subsystem 5 consumption.\n\nQualityObjects MUST declare:\n- evidence_ids\n- evidence_snapshot_id\n- policy_snapshot_id\n- comparison outcome\n- safety_disposition ∈ { SAFE_FOR_ACTION, REQUIRES_ESCALATION }\n\nAmbiguity, insufficiency, or conflict ⇒ REQUIRES_ESCALATION.\n\nSubsystem 5 may only approve actions when consuming QualityObjects\nthat are unambiguous, authoritative, and escalation-free.\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nIMPLEMENTATION CONSTRAINTS\n────────────────────────────────────────\n- Advisory data MUST NOT influence PQ, EC, comparisons, or rankings\n- Removing advisory functionality MUST NOT change behavior\n- All artifacts MUST validate schema_version strictly\n- All artifacts MUST bind determinism envelope inputs\n- All failures MUST map to authoritative stop-states\n\nEND OF TRANSFER BLOCK",
