                "snippet": "PROJECT CHARTER (AUTHORITATIVE)\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\nPROJECT NAME\nAletheia Forensis — The Reel Forensics Engine\n\nVERSION\nCore v1.0 (LOCKED)\n\nSTATUS\nCORE FORENSIC SYSTEM COMPLETE, VERIFIED, AND FINAL\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE\n2026-02-01\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nPURPOSE\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\nAletheia Forensis is a forensic-quality system for determining truth,\ncorrectness, and quality within a personal movie library.\n\nIts purpose is to:\n- determine what each video file actually contains\n- detect and explain errors (mislabels, duplicates, inferior versions)\n- rank versions by objective playback quality\n- produce trusted, reviewable outputs, including a canonical movie archive\n\nThe system analyzes, explains, and proposes — it never silently acts.\n\nAccuracy, determinism, and trust take precedence over automation.\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nPRIMARY OBJECTIVES (PRIORITY ORDER)\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\n1. Establish Truth\n   - What movie does each file represent?\n   - Is it mislabeled?\n   - Is it duplicate content?\n\n2. Enforce Correctness\n   - No two files containing the same movie content may exist under different names\n   - Mislabeling is always an error to be identified and corrected\n\n3. Assess Quality\n   - When multiple versions of the same movie exist, determine which is best by objective playback quality\n\n4. Produce Trusted Outputs\n   - Emit reviewable artifacts and proposed corrections\n   - Never silently mutate the library\n   - Preserve full provenance and determinism envelopes\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nCORE GOVERNANCE (ALWAYS IN FORCE)\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\n- Authoritative vs descriptive data:\n  Descriptive data (filenames/paths/metadata) must never drive decisions. Authoritative evidence prevails.\n\n- Determinism envelope (authoritative rule):\n  Outputs are deterministic only when these inputs are identical:\n  file_hash (or authoritative file_bytes), extractor_binary_hash, extractor_config_hash,\n  schema_version, policy_snapshot_id, evidence_snapshot_id,\n  model_hash (if used), advisory_retrieval_set_id (if referenced).\n  Any change => new evaluation => new artifact IDs.\n\n- Snapshot binding:\n  Every artifact must reference immutable evidence_snapshot_id and policy_snapshot_id.\n\n- Schema compatibility:\n  Every artifact must validate against the correct schema version.\n  Unsupported schema versions => HARD FAIL.\n\n- Stop-state algebra (authoritative set):\n  RESOLVED, UNKNOWN, UNKNOWN_PENDING, BLOCKED_HUMAN, CONFLICT, HALT_CONFLICT, HALT_STRUCTURAL.\n  No subsystem may invent new states. If no state applies => HARD FAIL.\n\n- Advisory non-authority (Subsystem 8 must obey):\n  Advisory outputs are strictly non-authoritative and must never influence identity, quality, dupe/mislabel,\n  safety, or termination decisions. Advisory may only be displayed/explained, not consumed as decision input.\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nSUBSYSTEM\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\nSUBSYSTEM: 8 — Advisory Intelligence Layer\nROLE: IMPLEMENTATION / HARDENING (NO DESIGN CHANGES to locked global governance)\n\nGOAL OF SUBSYSTEM 8:\n- Produce non-authoritative “advisory packets” for explanation / user-facing context only.\n- Prove formal inertness: advisory toggling cannot change authoritative termination output.\n- Enforce retrieval binding: if advisory references retrieval_set_ids, they must be explicitly provided and validated.\n- Enforce language guard: advisory text must not claim authority (“this is correct”, “final decision”, etc.).\n\nAUTHORITATIVE REPO STATE (from account memory snapshot):\n- src/aletheia_forensis is at: 57 directories, 382 files\n- Subsystem 8 (advisory) is implemented with:\n  build.py, cli.py, config.py, explain.py, hypotheses.py, ids.py, language_guard.py,\n  load.py, object.py, post_run.py, presentation.py, retrieval_binding.py,\n  retrieval_ids.py, retrieval_object.py, retrieval_validate.py, runner.py, validate.py\n  schemas: AdvisoryPacketSchema_1.json, RetrievalSetSchema_1.json\n  tests include inertness, CLI, retrieval binding enforcement, runtime wrapper inertness, schema immutability, etc.\n- Whole repo previously reported pytest passing 100% after Subsystem 8b hardening.\n\nLOCAL TREE CONFIRMED (example shown in prior chat):\n- tree -a -L 2 src/aletheia_forensis/advisory/tests shows current advisory tests set.\n\nCURRENT STATUS (SUBSYSTEM 8):\n- Subsystem 8 code exists and runs.\n- PYTHONPATH=src .venv/bin/pytest src/aletheia_forensis/advisory/tests -q: PASSING (100%) in latest successful runs.\n- CLI hardened to:\n  - validate and render only (no content generation, no live retrieval)\n  - require retrieval sets when referenced via --retrieval-map\n  - load retrieval sets as bytes and validate strictly\n  - enforce max bytes cap for retrieval set files (defense-in-depth)\n- Schema loader hardened:\n  - uses package resources\n  - enforces Draft 2020-12 via $schema\n  - enforces stable schema identity via $id (expected ids currently set to)\n    * https://aletheia-forensis/schemas/advisory/AdvisoryPacketSchema_1.json\n    * https://aletheia-forensis/schemas/advisory/RetrievalSetSchema_1.json\n  - check_schema enforced\n- Schema immutability test added with pinned BLAKE3:\n  - AdvisoryPacketSchema_1.json: 3f7bcda84400e429b6cd4afb77c9d430fbddfd0d94f8976aac0cf642dc305737\n  - RetrievalSetSchema_1.json:   bcfca96d97208ac70243ed1723c4579a9f3721c95129a8bb5e883412da48ff6a\n\nRECENT INCIDENT + RESOLUTION:\n- A test file was accidentally overwritten by a pasted block.\n- This was corrected; tests are passing again.\n- test_non_consumption.py briefly failed due to an incorrect “outside advisory” import scan logic;\n  it was corrected and now passes.\n\nWHAT IS LEFT / NEXT HARDENING STEP (NOT YET IMPLEMENTED):\n- Add an explicit “import boundary” t