                "snippet": "PROJECT: Imperium Aletheiae\nSYSTEM: Lex-Governed Financial Operations System\n\nCHAT: Chat 1b — Core Runtime & Determinism (IMPLEMENTATION)\nROLE: IMPLEMENTATION (STRICTLY BOUND BY LOCKED GOVERNANCE + LOCKED DESIGN)\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nAUTHORITATIVE MISSION STATEMENT\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\nTo create AI-powered systems that operate, adapt, and improve complex real-world infrastructure under strict human approval and oversight.\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nAUTHORITATIVE GOVERNANCE STATUS (NON-NEGOTIABLE)\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\nArtifacts 1–10 are COMPLETE, LOCKED, and IMMUTABLE.\nThey define:\n- authoritative schemas (including TerminalOutput)\n- authority boundaries\n- approval / audit / halt semantics\n- allowed stop states\n- validation requirements\n- immutability and persistence rules\n\nImplementation MUST bind to Artifacts 1–10 by immutable identifiers (IDs/hashes).\nNo “latest”, no floating references.\n\nIf the immutable IDs/hashes are not available at implementation time:\n- STOP and escalate (do not invent placeholders)\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nAUTHORITATIVE STOP-STATE ALGEBRA (LOCKED)\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\nStopState ENUM (closed set):\n  RESOLVED\n  UNKNOWN\n  UNKNOWN_PENDING\n  BLOCKED_HUMAN\n  CONFLICT\n  HALT_CONFLICT\n  HALT_STRUCTURAL\n\nPrecedence (strongest → weakest):\n  HALT_STRUCTURAL\n  HALT_CONFLICT\n  CONFLICT\n  BLOCKED_HUMAN\n  UNKNOWN_PENDING\n  UNKNOWN\n  RESOLVED\n\nPropagation model:\n- Ordered fold over stage results\n- merge(a,b) = max_precedence(a,b)\n- No downgrades permitted\n- Short-circuit on HALT_STRUCTURAL or HALT_CONFLICT\n- Any inability to compute a valid stop-state → HALT_STRUCTURAL\n\nCONFLICT is ALWAYS TERMINAL in the Core Runtime.\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nLOCKED DESIGN REFERENCE (AUTHORITATIVE)\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\nCHAT: Chat