K\n- determinism_envelope_hash: non-null iff LOCKED, else null\n- pre_envelope_trace: canonical object, always present\n- pre_envelope_trace_hash: always present, cryptographic anchor (NOT a fake envelope hash)\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nSTAGE IDENTITY + TRACE (LOCKED)\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\nTerminalOutput must carry controlled stage identity:\n- lifecycle_state (enum)\n- substage (enum)\n- stage_instance object:\n    sequence_index (0-based)\n    stage_id (controlled, governance-owned registry or closed enum)\n    attempt = 0 (retries forbidden; attempt != 0 → HALT_STRUCTURAL)\n\nstop_state_trace must be an ordered list with immutable refs:\n- sequence_index, stage_id\n- emitted_stop_state (StopState|null)\n- failure_class (enum|null)\n- reason_code (enum|null)\n- artifact_refs (immutable IDs/hashes only)\n\nNo free-text reasoning drives behavior.\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nTERMINALOUTPUT (AUTHORITATIVE SINGLE-SCHEMA GUARANTEE)\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\nThere is exactly ONE TerminalOutput schema and it must be producible under all failures.\n\nMandatory invariants:\n- exactly one TerminalOutput per run\n- stop_state ∈ StopState enum\n- TerminalOutput validates against authoritative schema\n- catastrophic failure still yields schema-valid TerminalOutput (single schema design)\n\nPersistence:\n- TerminalOutput is always persisted\n- persisted artifacts are immutable\n- no overwrite, no deletion\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nWORKING MODE\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\n- Precision over speed\n- One invariant at a time\n- Determinism by construction\n- No speculative features\n- Hard-fail on any violation\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nIMPLEMENTATION START POINT (ORDERED)\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\nImplement in this order:\n1) lifecycle state machine + enforcement\n2) stop-state propagation function (pure, total, precedence-based)\n3)